      "math_academy_id": "e-4439",
      "problem": "Calculate the minor of the entry $b_{21}$ in the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273095/assets/631c471d5de708ad8c3226886fdaad53878da9c74f063581d70e2837a53533c6.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "The minor of $b_{21} = 3$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $3$ are removed: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273095/assets/8f0cf1e3a84563c4eccae17aa6bded74589ec4d9fe856a0ee6e4f189445f93b2.svg)\n\nSo, the minor of $b_{21}=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =2-35 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
